# Overlay performance

Opening a dialog/sheet must stay cheap. This class of lag has shipped more than once (loan detail, then New group).

## Bans

| Do not | Do this |
| --- | --- |
| `backdrop-blur` / `backdrop-filter` on modal scrims | Solid tint (`.modal-scrim`, `bg-black/35`) |
| `transition-all` on chrome that also uses blur (sidebar, dock) | Transition only `width` / `margin` |
| Defer **every** `ResponsiveModal` body | `deferBody` only for heavy trees (loan form/detail) |
| `$effect(() => armWhenOpen(open))` that resets `ready` on every run | Rising-edge / `armed` guard in `createOverlayContentReady` |
| `$effect` on open that re-runs from `prop ?? []` | `$derived` for fallbacks; `untrack()` for one-shot init |
| `{#await import()}` in an overlay body | `$effect` + `$state` component (LoanCreateModal). A new Promise every parent render remounts the child and can loop with child→parent writes, leaving the 3-bar skeleton up forever |
| `isolate` on full-viewport overlay wrappers | `z-index` already creates a stacking context |
| `content-visibility: hidden` (or `visibility`/`display`) on `.app-shell` while `overlay-open` | Keep painting the page under the solid scrim on desktop and mobile |

Light dialogs (New group, pickers, confirms) mount the real form on open. The 3-bar skeleton in `ResponsiveModal` means `deferBody` is on; do not leave it on for a name field.

## Heavy overlay pattern

Lazy-load the heavy child **inside** the modal (`import()` from `$effect` into `$state`, plus `createOverlayContentReady`). Do not hide a small form behind the shared shell skeleton. Do not `{#await import()}` in the snippet.

See `.agent/skills/overlay-performance/SKILL.md`.
